# The Room 1 rebuild loop's scratch: blind A/B pairs, regenerated every round.
# The renders themselves are committed under renders/room-01-loop/.
work/

# RAW ROOM-PROOF CAPTURES. Tyler's policy: a full-resolution automated proof
# frame is a TEST ARTIFACT, not a canonical render. Shipping art and authored
# renders stay tracked; these do not.
#
# A 1920x1080 frame is ~2.9MB and a proof takes five or six, so forty rooms is
# roughly 700MB of blobs git deltas badly against a 279MB repository -- and
# every one of them is reproduced by `npm run proof <room>` in minutes.
#
# WHAT IS COMMITTED CARRIES THE CLAIMS: proof.json holds each capture's sha256,
# the commit, the state, the assets, the actor measurements and the route, and
# one compact four-panel sheet shows every COMPLETE frame beside it. A hash the
# next capture can be compared against proves more than a stored copy does.
renders/proofs/**/raw-captures-ignored/

# STAGED GENERATED IMAGES. Same shape as the proof captures above: the blobs
# are ignored, the claims about them are tracked.
#
# Nothing under art/staging/ has been looked at by Tyler, and a staged image is
# by definition not shipping art -- promotion is the only route into
# art/backgrounds/, it is explicit, and it is logged. Committing the staging
# area would put unaccepted generations in the same tree as accepted ones,
# which is the one distinction the whole staging layer exists to hold.
#
# art/staging/ledger.json and art/staging/caps.json stay TRACKED and are
# excepted below. The ledger is the provenance record AND the spend meter --
# budgetFor() computes attempts and billed tokens from its rows, so dropping it
# would silently reset every cap to zero.
art/staging/**
!art/staging/ledger.json
!art/staging/caps.json
# ROOM 5 PILOT CANDIDATES ARE REVIEWABLE, so they are tracked. Tyler's ruling:
# "Keep candidate artifacts reviewable." The composition master, the untouched
# API sources, the derived plate and Winnie's source are what he reviews, and
# what the proof loads by path -- a branch without them could reproduce
# neither. The ignore rule above stays for throwaway staging (the smoke test).
!art/staging/room-05/
!art/staging/room-05/**
